0..78 Comment "// The globular theory at dimension one, its associator a stated law, modelled"
79..104 Comment "// by the circle\'s paths."
105..107 Comment "//"
108..182 Comment "// A stated law is the theory\'s generator cell: no rule orients it, and no"
183..255 Comment "// default fills its component. The Path reading is a model of the cells"
256..312 Comment "// reading, so `math.path`\'s associator writes the cell."
313..315 Comment "//"
316..394 Comment "// The model writes the right unit law by conversion and the associator by the"
395..479 Comment "// theorem. A model leaving the associator out has it discharged by `Path.here`: the"
480..524 Comment "// two nestings of a chain of paths convert."
525..527 Comment "//"
528..610 Comment "// - see: `pathological/higher-cells/path-cells.gandr` — a model of the naturals"
611..671 Comment "//   leaving the cell out, and a scope breaking a stated law"
672..746 Comment "// - see: `cat-shape.gandr` — the same theory with its associator a rule"
748..795 Comment "// `assoc`, the associator of path composition."
796..802 Keyword "import"
803..804 StringLit "\""
804..840 StringLit "../../../library/math/src/path.gandr"
840..841 StringLit "\""
841..842 Other ";"
